Q: How to separate admin and user in codeigniter? A: <p>I solve this by setting the users permissions in a session variable when logging them in.</p>

<pre><code>$data = ['is_admin'     =&gt; true];
$this-&gt;session-&gt;set_userdata($data);
</code></pre>

<p>Then in the controllers for the admin area I do a check in the <code>__constructor()</code> method</p>

<pre><code>    /**
     * login protect
     */
    public function __construct()
    {
        if (!$this-&gt;session-&gt;userdata('is_admin')) {
            redirect('admin/account/login');
        }
    }
</code></pre>

